              "label": "WHY DOES A SIZE-K HEAP HELP?",
              "placeholder": "",
              "required": true,
              "reveal": {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When K is much smaller than n, you do not need to retain or sort every item. For the K largest items, keep a min-heap of the current winners; the root is the smallest winner and therefore the cutoff to beat.",
                "progressive_reveal": {
                  "spans": [
